From: Christopher Johannimloh
Subject: node_device_udev: fix deadlock joining udev thread under lock

Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://www.mail-archive.com/devel@lists.libvirt.org/msg17492.html]
Fixes: e89d39f5b8f30f0b3284ed2bd71cee1a8a3d707d

The shutdown thread must not hold the udevEventData lock while joining the
udev thread. The udev thread needs that lock to observe udevThreadQuit and
exit, otherwise libvirt reaches its 30 second forced-shutdown timeout.

diff --git a/src/node_device/node_device_udev.c b/src/node_device/node_device_udev.c
index 104433fb88..28c8f00361 100644
--- a/src/node_device/node_device_udev.c
+++ b/src/node_device/node_device_udev.c
@@ -2485,4 +2485,2 @@ nodeStateShutdownWait(void)
-    VIR_WITH_OBJECT_LOCK_GUARD(priv) {
-        if (priv->udevThread)
-            virThreadJoin(priv->udevThread);
-    }
+    if (priv->udevThread)
+        virThreadJoin(priv->udevThread);
